  "user_id": 18602,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Build a Loot-Opening Loop with AI\r\n\r\nYou're a Game Engineer working on a Minecraft-style dungeon loot system. The game is built, but one piece is missing: the loop that opens chests until a diamond is found.\r\n\r\nThe program should:\r\n- open one chest at a time with `openChest()`\r\n- save the item that comes back\r\n- check the item with `isDiamond(item)`\r\n- stop when the item is a diamond\r\n\r\nMost chests contain common items like bone or string. When the program finds a diamond, the victory screen should show.\r\n\r\n**Your job:**\r\n\r\n:::details [**1. Plan your prompt**]\r\nFill in the ROPE Plan in `prompt.md` before using AI Tutor.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**2. Prompt AI Tutor**]\r\nAsk AI Tutor to help you write a `while` loop. Include:\r\n- the helper functions: `openChest()` and `isDiamond(item)`\r\n- the variable that stores the current item\r\n- the condition that should stop the loop\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**3. Verify the code**]\r\nCheck that the loop opens a new chest each time and stops when a diamond is found.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**4. Test it**]\r\nRun the game. If the dungeon collapses, the loop probably did not stop correctly.\r\n:::",
